34,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It appears the landscape of expertise is shifting; while we have an abundance of interest in modelling and code, our experienced phenotyping technicians have largely departed for industry.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"And I found out that shipping costs are going up, but the ministry is still helping with glasshouse fees! Also, the national repository is way faster now.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that catalogue-style projects tend to be more useful in the long run, while some mechanism-focused ones just... didn't really solve their main questions. Also, breeding colonies often cause delays.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's a mess. The spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks because of a lapsed contract, and three out of five field sites were hit by floods or fires. Total chaos.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The computing agreement now covers simulation and modelling at no charge, but animal-unit day rates have risen sharply. Also, the animal facility is accredited, but the glasshouses are fully booked.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are facing a paradox; we have the digital tools and the desire for modelling, yet we lack the technical hands for physical phenotyping.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, wait! You said the glasshouses are fully booked, but I saw the ministry is still paying for them! Does that mean we can't use them even if they're subsidized?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I suppose that's a problem. If the glasshouses are full, it doesn't matter if they are subsidized, right? It's like having a coupon for a store that's closed.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,Exactly. And don't forget the field sites are a disaster zone and the spectroscopy gear is unreliable. We can't fund something that relies on broken equipment or flooded fields.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"That is a correct assessment, Takumi. The subsidies are irrelevant if there is no physical capacity. We must prioritize projects that avoid these bottlenecks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must also consider the human cost; if we fund a project requiring phenotyping technicians, we may find ourselves with a plan but no one to execute it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"That's a really good point, Servas! So we need someone who can do the work themselves or maybe someone who uses those cool computer models instead?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I think the catalogue-style projects might be safer... since they seem to last longer and provide more value, even if the process is slow.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm with Daisuke on that. If the field sites are underwater and the labs are broken, a project that just catalogs data is way less likely to crash and burn.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree. Given the current state of the shared facilities and the staffing shortages, a project with a focus on data synthesis or simulation would be the most stable choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,It is heartening to see us reaching a consensus. We must seek a path that aligns the ambition of the research with the reality of our available resources.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm totally on board! Let's find a project that doesn't need a million fancy machines or a hundred people to help out. That sounds like the smartest way to go!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just hope the candidates we see next actually fit this... I'd hate for us to have to choose between two projects that both seem risky.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"We'll just have to be honest about the risks. If a project looks like it'll get bogged down in a flooded field or a broken lab, we vote against it. Simple.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,Precisely. We shall apply these factual constraints to the candidates with objectivity. Let us move to the final round and review the proposals.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
