59,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have four candidates: the Microbiome Atlas, Protein Folding Dynamics, Regeneration in Amphibians, and Plant Drought Signaling. Each presents a different relationship with our current constraints.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Ooh, the Microbiome Atlas sounds like a catalogue project! Daisuke said those are the most useful, and it uses a repository, which I found out is super fast now!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. The Microbiome Atlas seems to fit the catalogue style I saw in the closeout files, and it might be more stable than the others.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Wait, the Atlas needs soil samples from different climate zones. @Takumi, remember those field sites? If they're still flooded or on fire, that project is in trouble.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Actually, @Takumi, the Atlas collects samples across several zones; it is less dependent on a single site than a focused trial. However, the Protein Folding Dynamics project aligns perfectly with our free computing and modelling capacity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"The Protein Folding project is indeed attractive, but we must remember the spectroscopy suite's instability. If the laboratory spectroscopy is essential, we risk the same delays Takumi warned us about.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"Wait, you're right! If the spectroscopy machine is broken, the Protein Folding project will just be stuck waiting. That's not a good way to start!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the Amphibian project might be risky too. It uses breeding colonies, and I read that those often cause the most schedule overruns.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly. And the animal facility day rates are through the roof, according to Minako. That project is a money pit and a scheduling nightmare. I'm out on that one.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"I agree. The Plant Drought Signaling project is also problematic, as it requires greenhouse trials, and we know the glasshouses are currently booked solid.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have systematically eliminated the others. The Plant project lacks space, the Amphibian project lacks budget and time, and the Protein project lacks reliable equipment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"So that leaves the Microbiome Atlas! It's a catalogue, the repository is fast, and it doesn't need a glasshouse or a broken spectroscopy machine. It's the perfect pick!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much more confident about the Atlas now. It seems like the safest and most beneficial choice for everyone involved.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm sold. Even with the field site risks, it's a better bet than a project that's dead on arrival because of a full greenhouse or a broken machine. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I concur. The Microbiome Atlas is the only proposal that avoids our primary infrastructure bottlenecks while leveraging the improved repository turnaround. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare pleasure when a panel finds such harmony. I shall add my vote to the Microbiome Atlas, for it is the most prudent path forward.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I vote for the Microbiome Atlas too! It's the winner! Yay!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
